{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries meaningful signal for this task. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly measures image-only performance using the simplest possible setup (no aggregation, standard pretrained encoder), isolating the modality effect. Combined with the RNA baseline, this lets us assess each modality's individual contribution before investing in multimodal fusion. If image-only substantially outperforms or underperforms RNA-only, it reshapes the entire search strategy (e.g., whether multimodal is promising, which modality to prioritize for encoder upgrades). This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice given the sparse evidence: it reduces uncertainty about the single most consequential design axis (modality) before spending budget on finer-grained choices like encoder type, aggregation, or fusion strategy."
}

